{"schema":2,"commit":"ab5309197b0d76cb6093fe7e435be8e4715a5069","branch":"main","base_sha":"34fa59de24a2e682c08be77c675b01711a821780","message":"Add a Claude hook debug log and build plugins from source\n\nThe PostToolUse hook runs inside Claude Code, so `blamely record claude`\nhas nowhere to report: stdout/stderr is swallowed by the host, and a\npayload dropped before the POST never reaches the daemon either. Give\nthat path its own append-only log at ~/.blamely/claude-debug.log\n(internal/tools/claudedebug.go), stepping through payload, parse,\ntranscript, extract, branch, resolve, gentype, usage and post. Writes\nare best-effort and rotate at 4 MB, keeping cmdRecord's \"always exit 0\"\ncontract; BLAMELY_DEBUG_CLAUDE=0 disables them.\n\n`blamely log claude` now follows the database like the Gemini tracer\ninstead of printing an explanation and exiting, and --debug backfills and\nfollows the hook log alongside it — the only view of the runs that\nrecorded nothing.\n\nTwo silent failures the log exposed, now reported: postToDaemon returns\nnil when no daemon is listening, so a dropped edit used to read as \"ok\";\nand a transcript path that resolves to nothing left model, tokens and\ngen_type defaulted with no trace. TestMain pins the logger off for the\npackage so tests that don't isolate HOME can't append to the developer's\nown log.\n\nscripts/install.sh rebuild now also builds ../vscode-plugin and\n../intellij-plugin from this checkout and sideloads those artifacts, so\nthe dev loop installs the code under edit rather than the published\nbuild; --skip-plugins keeps the CLI-only behaviour. Installing a local\n.vsix needed a counterpart to install-jetbrains-zip, so\nInstallEditorExtensions grew a source-taking variant behind the new\nhidden `install-vsix` command. Plugin build output goes to a log and is\nshown only on failure — the gradle build spawns a headless IDE that\ndumps SEVERE stack traces even when it succeeds, which made a clean\nrebuild look broken.\